---
import { comparison } from '../../lib/comparison';
import { integrationsRoute } from '../../lib/connections';

// What CostCook connects to, on /features rather than on a page of its own.
//
// THE DEDICATED PAGE. Until 2026-10-12 this said two Coming rows and one
// shipped argument were not a page. The owner asked for one that day
// (/features/integrations, RC-78), and it now leads with four connections that
// work today (Stripe card payments, invoice email, e-signature, files) before
// the two Coming ones, so it does not read as a roadmap. This section stays as
// the area page's summary and links there; both read the /compare rows.
//
// THE ORDER IS THE ARGUMENT. Competitors lead an integrations page with logos.
// The honest thing CostCook has and they do not is that prices arrive without
// a connection at all, because the intake reads the paper the supplier already
// sends. So that goes first and the two in-flight connectors go second, where
// they read as additions rather than as the answer.
//
// EVIDENCE. The one-queue lede rests on RC-38 (the import dropzone accepts
// JPEG, PNG, WebP, PDF, CSV, XLSX and DOCX, with a paste control beside it)
// and RC-09 (staged until confirmed). The three cards that restated the
// getting-prices-in figure (five doors, review, unreadable) were cut,
// owner-approved 2026-10-11; the figure and the import items carry them.
// Square and QuickBooks are RC-45. QuickBooks is built and flag-gated on
// kitchen-brain develop 4f46543cf (FEATURE_QUICKBOOKS_INTEGRATION_ENABLED; the
// sandbox-only lock is gone), and stays Coming by the 2026-09-27 owner ruling
// (ledger RC-45 note, 2026-10-11). Square is built too: sandbox/demo carries the provider, catalog mapping, settings screens,
// the OAuth callback and the webhook, all of it behind
// integrationExecutionAllowed(businessId, 'square_integration',
// env.FEATURE_SQUARE_INTEGRATION_ENABLED), which defaults off. "Coming" is
// therefore true of the app a reader would start today and stays true only
// while that flag is off in production. If it is ever switched on for anyone,
// this section and the /compare row are both underclaiming and must move to
// Yes. Neither carries a date either way.
//
// The two Coming lines are read out of comparison.ts rather than retyped, so
// the /compare table and this section cannot say different things about the
// same connector.
const comingRows = comparison
	.flatMap((group) => group.rows)
	.filter((row) => row.label === 'Point of sale' || row.label === 'Accounting');
---

<!-- story: docs/stories/integrations.story.md -->
<section id="connections" class="mt-16 border-t border-ticket-rule pt-8" aria-labelledby="connections-heading">
	<div>
		<div class="max-w-3xl">
			<p class="eyebrow">What it connects to</p>
			<h2 id="connections-heading" class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">
				Your supplier does not have to be plugged in. CostCook reads the paper.
			</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[62ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
				There is no long list of connectors here because prices get in without
				one. An order guide, a price sheet, an invoice, or a photograph of a
				delivery slip taken on the loading dock all go through the same queue.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 max-w-3xl">
			<h3 class="text-h3 font-semibold">Square and QuickBooks are not available yet</h3>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-[62ch] text-ink-soft">
				Neither connection is included in the subscription today. No release date has been announced.
			</p>
			<ul role="list" class="mt-6 space-y-5">
				{
					comingRows.map((row) => (
						<li class="border-t border-hairline pt-4">
							<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
								<p class="font-semibold">{row.label}</p>
								<span class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-ticket-rule bg-softamber px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-deep">
									Coming
								</span>
							</div>
							<p class="mt-2 max-w-[62ch] text-ink-soft">{row.label === 'Point of sale' ? 'Square is not available today. You cannot send menus to your till or bring sales into CostCook through this connection.' : 'QuickBooks Online is not in the app you would start today, so CostCook does not sync your purchases or accounts with it.'}</p>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ul>
			<p class="mt-6">
				<a href={integrationsRoute} class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold text-green-deep underline decoration-ticket-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-green">Connect your tools: what works today, and what Square and QuickBooks will do</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
